wineaaudio.drv: An audio driver of Wine for Android, with AAudio.

Wine 11.0 has no audio driver for Android: winealsa, winepulse and wineoss
need what Android does not give an app, so mmdevapi finds no driver and a
program has no sound. This driver gives the output of mmdevapi (waveOut of
winmm, dsound, the IAudioClient of a program) to an AAudio stream of the
NDK (libaaudio, Android 8 and later) with a data callback. It has the form
of the unix side of dlls/wineoss.drv/oss.c, and the PE side is the empty
module of each driver of mmdevapi. The output is the one output device of
Android. There is no capture device and no MIDI device.

configure: the driver is built when the header aaudio/AAudio.h is there
and libaaudio links (the NDK, API 26 and later). The prefix selects it
with HKCU\Software\Wine\Drivers, "Audio" = "aaudio".

